Bela Fazekas <bela@magfiz.iki.kfki.hu> wrote:
>I look for somebody who can help me to solve the following problem:
>I compiled a fortran program with f77 and when I run the program
>I get the following messages several times:
>Unaligned access pid=2899 <cindy.exe> ...
>How can I suspend these run time messages without rewrite the program?
>In other words is there any switch in the compiler which suspends
>these messages?

You may be paying a massive performance penalty for this unaligned
access. Try re-compiling with some compiler option that will align data
on word (or double-word) boundaries. The option in DEC Fortran under
OSF/1 is either '-align commons' or '-align dcommons'.

For example:

	% f77 -align dcommons -o prog prog.f

See your compiler documentation for the details.

-Randy

