My guess is that lots of people thought they HAD discussed it,
but all the premature "I Vote Yes" messages were followups to
a different message.

I think that a DCE-related newsgroup of some sort is a good idea.
I disagree that the traffic is insufficient.  It is somewhat light,
but also spread out, with basic DCE questions being posted to
comp.client-server, comp.unix.osf.misc, and comp.unix.osf.osf1 (!),
(and possibly others that I don't usually read).  
I think there is a very real possibility that traffic would increase
if more people could find the proper forum.

Personally, I favor one of the alternate proposals:
    comp.distributed
which would likely have higher usage, since it would be a suitable home
for DCE, CORBA, message-passing, etc, and could be subdivided
at some point in the future, if necessary.  I think the distinction
between "distributed" and "client-server" is enough to justify the
new group, and I think that comp.client-server will not lack for
continued traffic discussing Powerbuilder and the adequacy of the
Gartner Group's C-S model.


