I think current patterns suggest

comp.dist.misc instead of comp.dist
comp.dist.corba
comp.dist.dce

Another possibility would be just 

comp.dist.misc

and wait for traffic patterns to shape later group boundaries.

Yet another possibility is

comp.dist.misc
comp.dist.object
comp.dist.rpc
comp.dist.msg

This split is meant to highlight that CORBA and DCE are in some sense
just today's representatives of a higher level architecture split.  For
example, most CORBA, Taligent, NEXTSTEP DO discussion would appear in
c.d.object.  ONC, NCS, DCE discussion in c.d.rpc.  RQS, RTR, /Q
discussion in c.d.msg

