|>Gerhard Rentschler (zrsl0136@sysger.rus.uni-stuttgart.de) wrote:
|>: Hi,
|>: I have a very special problem with dce. cdscp list clearinghouse shows
|>: a clearinghouse on a machine which no longer exists. How can I get rid
|>: of it? cdscp delete clearinghouse wants to talk to this machine and
|>: fails if it doesn't get a response. Is there some file to edit?

	I ran into a similar situation a while back when one of the
	machines housing a CDS replica was taken off the cell without my
	knowledge.  Anyways, you will not be able to delete it using
	"delete clearinghouse."  However, you can fool CDS by deleting
	it as an object.  Try "cdscp delete object /.:/DEAD_CH."

	Keep in mind that the directories which were in your old CH
	will still exist in the namespace but they will not be accessible
	unless they were replicated in another CH.

|>Try this:
|>cdscp>set directory /.:/ to new epoch master /.:/master_ch \
|>>exclude /.:/old_ch

	This still will not remove the dead CH entry in CDS.

