Is it possible with DCE to have the login credentials associated
with a person instead of a login name?  What we would like to have
are multiple login names/accounts associated with one person, but
only have one authority entry that verifies this person.

For example, if I want to install a product on one of our computers
I would like to login to a different account from my normal user
account. This allows me to keep these job functions separate. I can't
then accidentally delete files belonging to myself or to the product,
because the account permissions will protect me.  I can build the
product and track the resource usage of these activities. Also, the
separate account id will allow me to know how much disk resource is being
used by the product.

I would like my login credential to be the owner of all these accounts
for security reasons. I want the accounts to be tied to a person, thus
making the account auditable, and for that person to have one password
that that is retrieved from the login credential, not from the account.
I don't want the user to have to remember multiple passwords.

If there are other ways to handle this, I'd be interested also.


