	INTERNATIONAL
	    DCE
	 USERS GROUP 


	PRESS RELEASE
Contact: Harold Lockhart, (617)577-9196 ext. 1208 hlockhar@onsett.com

Boston, MA  August 31, 1994 -A group of users of the Open Software Foundation's
Distributed Computing Environment (DCE) has formed the International DCE Users 
Group (IDUG), they announced today at the OSF DCE Developers Conference held in 
Boston.

The IDUG is open to any computer professional and is not affiliated with OSF or 
any other organization.  "Its purpose is to provide a forum for exchange of 
information among those who are applying DCE technology and ultimately to 
influence vendor products supporting the technology," said Harold Lockhart, a 
consultant with Onsett International Corporation, Cambridge, MA and one of the 
organizers of the new group.

"DCE is a very important step forward in enabling distributed computing but 
distributed computing is not an easy proposition and DCE users are in many 
respects pioneers." Lockhart said.  He said he expects that IDUG initially will 
be valuable as a resource for DCE related information including listings of new 
products and services that support DCE, as a channel of communication to expert 
advice.  "There will also be a role for users to play in setting specifications 
for DCE-enabled products," he said. Lockhart is author of OSF DCE: Guide to 
Developing Distributed Applications, published by McGraw-Hill this year.

The group will primarily function as a clearinghouse for information.  However, 
it will liaison with the many local DCE users groups which are springing up in 
different parts of the world.  In future, the IDUG may also get involved in 
organizing regional forums, trade shows and seminars; creating a DCE lab for 
interoperability and benchmark testing; and stimulating research and development
in DCE-related areas, he said.

"This is an exciting opportunity for members of the wider IT community who are 
interested in DCE but are not necessarily OSF members at this time," said Bill 
Estrem of the 3M Corporation,  "however, I expect that many OSF members will 
join this new organization as well."

IDUG has set a per contact, annual membership fee of $25.  Inquiries can be 
directed to 

