In article <342f68$4cm@hawk.anselm.edu> rdumont@hawk.anselm.edu (Ron Dumont) writes:
> Has anyone found a good autologout script or program that
> runs on OSF/1? 
> 
> The ideal would be something that searches for idle users
> (initiated by cron) vs. a program that is run within a
> login script that times users and kills all associated 
> processes after a specified inactivity setting (i.e. tout).
> 
> Thanks in advance.

If you add the line

export TMOUT=1800	# thirty minutes (30 * 60)

to /etc/profile, all ksh users will be logged out automatically after
30 minutes (or whatever period you specify) of inactivity.  The csh
and sh do not have this capability, though csh can be replaced with
tcsh which does ("set autologout=30").  These solutions do not require
a separate process at all.

