Steve Melchert (smelch01@cps.plnin.gmeds.com) wrote:
: I would like to capture the IP address of a calling client from the 
: server layer.  I want this information so that I can store certain
: information related to specific IP's.  Is it part of the context
: handle?  Can it be captured?

: I have been told that there is no API to directly obtain this data.
: Does anyone have any idea how to capture the IP address from the server?
: Would like to avoid a lot of messy code if possible, as my product is
: to be cross-platform portable.

: Thanks for any input you can provide.

: Stephen Melchert

Steve,

You can use a combination of rpc_binding_server_from_client and 
rpc_binding_to_string_binding to get the information according
to the documentation.  The rpc_binding_server_from_client call 
only provides a partially bound handle so you will not have
an endpoint for the client but you will have the IP address.

Hope this helps.

Jim
