> Episode as backing store. 

Now you're asking about JFS.  Are you asking about NFS-exporting or
DFS-exporting? 

There's an obvious semantic problem about exporting anything via NFS, in
that your clients will get the least-common-denominator consistency
rather than the tight consistency available when DFS exporting is done
alone.  And it could be that the multiple exporting (via DFS and NFS
both) isn't heavily tested in last summer's IBM product for DCE. 

I don't believe that the existing HP-UX DCE provides Episode at all (yet). 

Of course, if you wanted to quote the ``state-consistency hazard''
description that you've seen, that would be useful, since we might be
able to explain what was going on behind that description. 

